# Build phases

Follow the Campus Plug build checklist. Do not start a later phase while an earlier gate is open. Do not build screens during backend work.

0. Site prep — accounts, repo, Supabase link, `.env`, Expo Go.
1. Backend — migrations, RLS, RPCs, storage, Edge Functions, types. Gate: `npx supabase db push` applies cleanly and every check in `supabase/tests/rls_checks.md` passes.
2. App shell and auth — tokens, shared components, Expo Router groups `(auth)`, `(tabs)`, `admin`. Gate: sign up, log in, stay logged in after restart, tabs match `profiles.role`.
3. Marketplace — vendor apply, products, photos, home, `search_products`, shop page. Gate: an approved vendor lists a product and a buyer finds it.
4. Orders and chat — `get_or_create_conversation`, Realtime, `place_order`, status transitions. Gate: buyer places an order, vendor accepts, both see live updates.
5. Profile, notifications, account — avatar, dev build for Android push, inbox, `delete-account`.
6. Admin — review, remove, moderate, audit log. UI guard plus existing RLS.
7. Inspection — buyer, vendor, and admin on two phones; advisors; no service role in the app.
8. Release prep — `app.json` identity, EAS profiles, privacy URLs, store listings.
9. Opening day — vendors first, then buyers.
10. After launch — rank feedback, then v2 (Paystack, alarms, events, vendor monetization). Buyer requests are part of v1.

MVP stays cash on delivery, currency GHS. Stop after a phase gate and report what is still open.

When payments start, vendor verification is a Paystack monthly subscription in GHS. Admin approval stays free and is what lets a shop list. The verified badge shows only when the shop is approved and the subscription is active. An Edge Function webhook is the only writer of that status. The app opens Paystack checkout and never stores card or Mobile Money details. A failed payment keeps the shop and its products, hides the badge, and allows a short grace period before the badge drops. Start with one monthly price, not tiers. Do not take a cut of cash-on-delivery orders.
